  "files": [
    {
      "path": "index.html",
      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Pixel Temperature Converter</title>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"card\">\n  <h1 class=\"title\">PIXEL TEMP CONVERTER</h1>\n  <p class=\"formula\">C&rarr;F: x&times;9/5+32 &nbsp;|&nbsp; F&rarr;C: (x&minus;32)&times;5/9</p>\n\n  <label for=\"temperature\" class=\"label\">Temperature</label>\n  <input id=\"temperature\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" placeholder=\"e.g. 100\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n\n  <label for=\"direction\" class=\"label\">Direction</label>\n  <select id=\"direction\">\n    <option value=\"c-to-f\">Celsius &rarr; Fahrenheit</option>\n    <option value=\"f-to-c\">Fahrenheit &rarr; Celsius</option>\n  </select>\n\n  <button id=\"convert\" type=\"button\">CONVERT</button>\n\n  <div class=\"output-wrap\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n    <span class=\"output-label\">Result</span>\n    <span id=\"result\">--</span>\n  </div>\n</main>\n<script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "style.css",
      "content": ":root {\n  --bg: #1b1b2f;\n  --panel: #2a2a45;\n  --accent: #ffcc00;\n  --text: #f4f4f8;\n  --muted: #9a9ab5;\n}\n\n* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n\nbody {\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  padding: 20px;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  background-image:\n    linear-gradient(45deg, #23233a 25%, transparent 25%),\n    linear-gradient(-45deg, #23233a 25%, transparent 25%),\n    linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 75%, #23233a 75%),\n    linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent 75%, #23233a 75%);\n  background-size: 24px 24px;\n  background-position: 0 0, 0 12px, 12px -12px, -12px 0;\n  font-family: \"Courier New\", ui-monospace, monospace;\n  color: var(--text);\n  font-size: 16px;\n}\n\n.card {\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: 420px;\n  background: var(--panel);\n  border: 4px solid var(--accent);\n  box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 #000;\n  padding: 28px 24px;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 12px;\n}\n\n.title {\n  font-size: 1.25rem;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n  text-align: center;\n  color: var(--accent);\n}\n\n.formula {\n  font-size: 0.8rem;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  text-align: center;\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n}\n\n.label {\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n}\n\ninput, select {\n  font-family: inherit;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  padding: 12px;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--text);\n  border: 3px solid var(--muted);\n  width: 100%;\n}\n\ninput:focus, select:focus {\n  outline: none;\n  border-color: var(--accent);\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(255, 204, 0, 0.35);\n}\n\nbutton {\n  font-family: inherit;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  font-weight: bold;\n  letter-spacing: 2px;\n  padding: 14px;\n  margin-top: 8px;\n  color: var(--bg);\n  background: var(--accent);\n  border: 3px solid var(--accent);\n  box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #000;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: transform 0.05s, box-shadow 0.05s, background 0.15s;\n}\n\nbutton:hover { background: #ffe066; }\n\nbutton:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid var(--text);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n\nbutton:active {\n  transform: translate(4px, 4px);\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 #000;\n}\n\n.output-wrap {\n  margin-top: 12px;\n  padding: 16px;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  border: 3px dashed var(--muted);\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 6px;\n}\n\n.output-label {\n  font-size: 0.8rem;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n}\n\n#result {\n  font-size: 1.75rem;\n  font-weight: bold;\n  color: var(--accent);\n  word-break: break-all;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 400px) {\n  .card { padding: 20px 16px; }\n  .title { font-size: 1.05rem; }\n  #result { font-size: 1.4rem; }\n}\n",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "script.js",
      "content": "(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n\n  var input = document.getElementById(\"temperature\");\n  var direction = document.getElementById(\"direction\");\n  var button = document.getElementById(\"convert\");\n  var result = document.getElementById(\"result\");\n\n  function convert() {\n    var raw = input.value.trim();\n    var value = raw === \"\" ? NaN : Number(raw);\n\n    if (!isFinite(value)) {\n      result.textContent = \"Error\";\n      return;\n    }\n\n    var out;\n    if (direction.value === \"c-to-f\") {\n      out = value * 9 / 5 + 32;\n    } else {\n      out = (value - 32) * 5 / 9;\n    }\n\n    result.textContent = out.toFixed(2);\n  }\n\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", convert);\n\n  input.addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (e) {\n    if (e.key === \"Enter\") {\n      convert();\n    }\n  });\n})();\n",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Temperature Converter\n\nA fully offline, pixel-styled temperature converter built with plain HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript. No packages, no network requests, no storage.\n\n## Features\n\n- Convert Celsius to Fahrenheit and Fahrenheit to Celsius\n- Exact two-decimal numeric output (no units)\n- Empty or invalid/non-finite input shows `Error`\n- Result starts at `--`\n- Keyboard accessible: labeled controls, visible focus states, Enter key triggers conversion\n- Responsive layout down to 360px wide\n\n## Formulas\n\n- Celsius to Fahrenheit: `x * 9/5 + 32`\n- Fahrenheit to Celsius: `(x - 32) * 5/9`\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Enter a numeric temperature in the **Temperature** field.\n3. Choose a direction in the **Direction** dropdown (`c-to-f` or `f-to-c`).\n4. Click **CONVERT** (or press Enter) to see the result.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` — page structure and required IDs (`temperature`, `direction`, `convert`, `result`)\n- `style.css` — pixel-art theme, palette, responsive layout, control states\n- `script.js` — conversion logic and input validation\n- `README.md` — this documentation\n\n## Notes\n\n- Output is always formatted with exactly two decimals using `toFixed(2)`.\n- Input is parsed with `Number()`; whitespace-only or non-numeric input yields `Error`.\n- No external assets, iframes, or server code are used.\n",
      "description": ""
    }
  ]
}